From 8f553186ca7d50fb20ecda60207cb0a9a19c9a31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dugs <dugahol@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:17:19 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 31/33] input: apple-z2: document that poll_hz>0 wedges the D21
 controller

Measured 2026-10-30: with poll_hz=120 the off-IRQ pulls return all-zero
(1258 of 1303), the frame stream collapses from 24 fps to ~1 Hz with
phantom storms, and the wedge survives rmmod + reload + 45 s rails-off -
same persistence class as the dma_min/ip_delay poisoning, force-restart
is the only recovery.  iOS never pulls without an IRQ, so there is no
RE'd contract for empty pulls; the D21 runtime firmware clearly does not
serve them.  The Orchard j71b poller pattern does not transfer.

Also fixes a comment typo that truncated a block comment (rtpoll_*/...).
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
index 57103ccb5..48531024f 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
@@ -1537,13 +1537,18 @@ static irqreturn_t apple_z2_irq(int irq, void *data)
 
 /*
  * Orchard-style runtime poller rate in Hz (0 = off, the default).  See
- * apple_z2_d21_poll_work().  60-120 is a sensible range; values above the
- * SPI command round-trip just burn bus time on empty pulls.
+ * apple_z2_d21_poll_work().  WARNING (measured 2026-10-30): non-zero values
+ * WEDGE the D21 controller - off-IRQ pulls return all-zero and the frame
+ * stream collapses to ~1 Hz with phantom storms; the wedge survives
+ * reload + 45 s rails-off and needs a force-restart, like the dma_min
+ * poisoning.  Kept for the record; do not enable on D21.
  */
 static unsigned int d21_poll_hz;
 module_param_named(poll_hz, d21_poll_hz, uint, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(poll_hz,
-		 "D21: poll the frame queue at N Hz instead of trusting per-frame IRQs (0=off)");
+		 "D21: poll the frame queue at N Hz instead of trusting per-frame IRQs "
+		 "(0=off). WARNING: non-zero wedges the controller (persists across reloads, "
+		 "force-restart to recover)");
 
 /*
  * Orchard-style runtime poller (j71b_z2.ko runs its whole runtime POLLED,
